<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">National anthem of Russia (words by Sergey Mikhalkov)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2000</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Derzhavny Soyuz Narodov (proposed anthem of the State Union of Russia and Belarus)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new words (never adopted)</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hymn of the Bolshevik Party (Alexander Alexandrov)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1938</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same music, first composed for it</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Life Has Become Better (Alexander Alexandrov)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">after 1935</span><span class="sg-chain-h">opening bars borrowed</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bylina, Epic Poem (Vasily Kalinnikov, overture)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">shares several chord progressions (possible influence)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Frühlingsfahrt (Robert Schumann)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">similarities noted (possible influence)</span></li></ul></section>
